      "writtenOn": "2021-03-02T11:55:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, I tried. I came up with these patches to make these tests work:\n\nhttps://paste.googleplex.com/5373575897808896\nhttps://paste.googleplex.com/6165098910449664\n\nbut they are excessively ugly and then after this, the tests will say\n\nFAILED: .bootstrap/blueprint-parser/test/test.a\nGOROOT\u003d\u0027/usr/lib/google-golang\u0027 /usr/lib/google-golang/pkg/tool/linux_amd64/compile -c 8 -o .bootstrap/blueprint-parser/test/test.a.tmp -p main -complete -I ./.bootstrap/blueprint-parser/test -pack .bootstrap/blueprint-parser/test/test.go \u0026\u0026 if cmp --quiet .bootstrap/blueprint-parser/test/test.a.tmp .bootstrap/blueprint-parser/test/test.a; then rm .bootstrap/blueprint-parser/test/test.a.tmp; else mv -f .bootstrap/blueprint-parser/test/test.a.tmp .bootstrap/blueprint-parser/test/test.a; fi\n.bootstrap/blueprint-parser/test/test.go:82:36: cannot use matchString{} (type matchString) as type testing.testDeps in argument to testing.MainStart:\n        matchString does not implement testing.testDeps (missing SetPanicOnExit0 method)\n[19/37] compile .bootstrap/blueprint-pathtools/test/test.a\n\nGiven that the shell magic will go away with aosp/1609218 anyway, I recommend not worrying about Blueprint\u0027s tests now and resurrect them once these refactorings are done.\n\nWDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "6f7e4ba1_c2c6c92a",
      "revId": "b7679d96fbd01caaae31d0b18aa9bea6579a6911",
