        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-08T16:43:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are there any particular scenarios you are concerned about? My line of reasoning that I\u0027m making the bootstrapping process much simpler (see: re-running Android.bp parsing on null builds), so the incrementality story is much simpler.",
      "parentUuid": "1f073f58_2a12edd0",
      "revId": "b7679d96fbd01caaae31d0b18aa9bea6579a6911",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc229322_215261a3",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-08T17:18:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the performance is deemed inadequate, I could do two things:\n\n1. Hand-roll a way to rebuild .bootstrap/build.ninja iff a Blueprint file was changed/added/removed or a glob file changed. This is extra hand-rolled logic and is certainly more error-prone than no logic.\n\n2. Invoke soong_ui itself using a tiny Ninja file. This would make it harder to debug the generation of .bootstrap/build.ninja and would be an extra step.\n\nI would lean towards (1) if I had to choose one because I hope it results in a simpler overall code flow. We don\u0027t even need to add a Go .d file parser (if we don\u0027t have one already, I don\u0027t know) because we can tell the Blueprint invocation generating .bootstrap/build.ninja to emit the contents of the .d file in some even simpler \"one file name per line\" format that\u0027s trivial to parse.",
      "parentUuid": "0f3874de_3bfb8d83",
      "revId": "b7679d96fbd01caaae31d0b18aa9bea6579a6911",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
